# Context

## Background
T050 implements the calibrate API of MVP_SPEC.md sections 5, 7-8, and 11.
T047-T049 delivered the Rust plan contract, the bounded fitting search, and
the frozen validation, but no Node binding exposed them, so the library had
no way to run a calibration. The prior session (a5a1fcf) shipped the
surrounding wrapper parts (evaluate, CLI, fixtures); this commit completes
the operation itself.

## Why This Way
- The fitting search and the frozen validation cross as napi `Task`
  implementations, so `compute` runs on one libuv worker thread. This keeps
  the bounded calculations (up to 1,048,576 policy decisions) off the Node
  event loop with no tokio dependency and no callback into user code, which
  MVP_SPEC.md section 5 requires.
- `qualifyCandidate` re-runs the deterministic search over the same fitting
  assessments instead of taking a serialized fit report: `FitReport` holds
  `&'static str` fields and a `#[serde(skip)]` confusion matrix, so
  deserializing it would need invasive core changes, and the freeze checks
  of the core already re-verify every identity.
- The measurement runs go through `createExplorationProfile` plus a public
  `load`, served through one delegating file access at a synthetic
  `measuretwice://...json` path. This reuses the validated execution path
  (bounds, retries, deadline, cancellation) instead of writing a second
  scheduler, and the starter policy of the measurement profile never reaches
  the candidate: the search replays the stored assessments.
- The host must state `evaluationReports` because the profile contract
  requires the complete evidence set for one calibration origin and the host
  owns report storage. The wrapper invents no storage path.

## Gotchas
- `calibrate` refuses with the record's own operational code when one
  measured case stores no assessment, and with `model_resolution_changed`
  when the measurements resolved two model versions: one calibration
  measures with one model.
- One plan whose selection names an undeclared split refuses in the wrapper
  with the core split-locator wording, because no identity exists for the
  core to compare.
- The scheduler admission loop now stops after a run that ended during
  admission; without that guard, one caller abort stated from inside the
  first attempt made the loop offer the next check to a frozen run state.

